{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["Give strength, Father of multitudes, to HaShem and give thanks, when you arrive at the beginning of \"These are the reckonings of\"" "<b>These are the reckonings.</b> The meaning: the reckonings of the vessels, for the word משכן encompasses everything. And he explained why it is called mishkan: on account of the ark, where the tablets of testimony are, and behold he held to a concise path, and this is the truth, on account of the inscription of Elohim." "<b>And the meaning of \"the service of the Levites.\"</b> That they carry the mishkan and all its vessels, which was appointed over them by Itamar; for the Gershonites and the Merarites, the Levites, were under the hand of Itamar, who would reckon by names all of their burdens:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:50.100371108Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}